WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.356 --> 00:00:01.755
Welcome to Cyrus.

2
00:00:01.755 --> 00:00:06.250
This is the Overview, the page you land on every time you open the app.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.445
It pulls together every exchange you've connected, so

4
00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:12.580
you can see your whole crypto picture in one place.

5
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:18.692
Everything you're seeing here is demo data, but it behaves exactly like a real account.

6
00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:25.048
In this one, four exchanges are connected: Kraken, Coinbase, Binance and Robinhood.

7
00:00:25.716 --> 00:00:27.381
Let's start at the very top.

8
00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:29.868
The search box takes you to any page.

9
00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:35.041
Press the slash key, type a few letters, like 'tax', and press Enter.

10
00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:38.112
Next to it is the exchange selector.

11
00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:43.139
On All Exchanges, every number in the app is combined across your accounts.

12
00:00:43.139 --> 00:00:47.314
Pick a single account, and every page narrows to just that one.

13
00:00:47.996 --> 00:00:51.111
Now we're only looking at the Kraken account called Main.

14
00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:56.005
The portfolio, the orders and the caps have all been recalculated for it.

15
00:00:56.005 --> 00:00:57.773
Let's switch back to everything.

16
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.864
The worker pill shows that the automation engine is running,

17
00:01:01.864 --> 00:01:04.424
and how recently it last checked your rules.

18
00:01:04.424 --> 00:01:08.214
It runs quietly in the background, about once a minute.

19
00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:13.393
Underneath, a ticker scrolls through your portfolio total and live prices

20
00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:17.339
for the coins you hold, with the day's change next to each one.

21
00:01:18.015 --> 00:01:25.896
Back on the page, the headline numbers give you the essentials at a glance: what everything's worth, how much it moved in the last

22
00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:33.656
twenty-four hours, how many orders are working, how many automations you have, and whether any coin is over its allocation cap.

23
00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.245
Each tile is also a shortcut.

24
00:01:36.245 --> 00:01:39.849
Clicking one takes you straight to the page with the full detail.

25
00:01:40.525 --> 00:01:43.613
The portfolio ring shows how your money is split.

26
00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:47.011
Each slice is a coin, sized by its dollar value, and

27
00:01:47.011 --> 00:01:50.475
the smaller positions are grouped together as Other.

28
00:01:50.475 --> 00:01:52.151
The total sits in the middle.

29
00:01:52.828 --> 00:01:54.879
Beside it is a live price chart.

30
00:01:54.879 --> 00:02:00.424
Choose a pair from the list, and pick a time range, from the last hour up to the last year.

31
00:02:01.086 --> 00:02:04.250
Add Crypto puts another coin on your watch list, so you

32
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.126
can follow a price even if you don't hold it yet.

33
00:02:07.781 --> 00:02:12.772
Scrolling down, Biggest Holdings lists your largest positions with a small price

34
00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:17.452
trend, the current price, the day's move, and what each position is worth.

35
00:02:18.128 --> 00:02:25.217
Resting Limit Orders splits your orders into buys and sells, with the total value on each side, then

36
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:32.094
lists the most recent ones: the pair, the account, the price, the amount and when it was placed.

37
00:02:32.758 --> 00:02:37.681
Allocation Caps shows each coin against the share of your account you've allowed it.

38
00:02:37.681 --> 00:02:39.596
The bar fills toward the cap.

39
00:02:39.596 --> 00:02:43.253
When a coin goes over, the bar turns amber, and Cyrus tells

40
00:02:43.253 --> 00:02:46.538
you how much it would trim to bring it back in line.

41
00:02:47.231 --> 00:02:50.865
Recent Activity is the automation log in miniature.

42
00:02:50.865 --> 00:02:56.120
Every run is recorded, including the ones that didn't trade, with a plain-English

43
00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.051
reason, like a coin being under its cap or a rule waiting out its cooldown.

44
00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:05.805
At the bottom, the Flow chart draws your automations as a map.

45
00:03:05.805 --> 00:03:11.723
Each circle is a coin, and each line is a rule that converts one coin into another.

46
00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:14.170
Dashed outlines are rules that are paused.

47
00:03:14.846 --> 00:03:17.968
Switch to Open Orders, and the same chart shows where your

48
00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:20.820
resting orders would take your money if they filled.

49
00:03:21.496 --> 00:03:23.733
Every widget can be rearranged.

50
00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:26.273
Scroll back up and click Customize.

51
00:03:26.948 --> 00:03:29.039
Each widget now has a toolbar.

52
00:03:29.039 --> 00:03:32.603
Drag the grip to move a widget, or use the arrows.

53
00:03:32.603 --> 00:03:36.060
The minus and plus buttons make it narrower or wider.

54
00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:41.499
The page is a twelve-column grid, and the counter shows how many columns a widget is using.

55
00:03:42.171 --> 00:03:45.312
Dragging the bottom-right corner resizes a widget.

56
00:03:45.312 --> 00:03:50.499
Its height can follow its content, or stay fixed with the content scrolling inside.

57
00:03:50.499 --> 00:03:56.323
Double-click the corner, or use the up-and-down arrow button, to make it fit its content again.

58
00:03:56.983 --> 00:03:59.340
Add Widget opens the full list.

59
00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.445
Besides the ones you've seen, there's Top Movers, an Accounts summary, Recent

60
00:04:04.445 --> 00:04:08.821
Transfers, Quick Actions, and a Notes pad for your own reminders.

61
00:04:09.494 --> 00:04:10.987
Let's add Top Movers.

62
00:04:10.987 --> 00:04:15.175
It lists the holdings that rose or fell the most over the last day.

63
00:04:15.927 --> 00:04:18.483
Your layout saves to your account as you go.

64
00:04:18.483 --> 00:04:21.994
If you ever want the original back, Reset restores it.

65
00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.922
When you're finished, click Done.

66
00:04:24.612 --> 00:04:28.722
The refresh button reloads everything from your exchanges straight

67
00:04:28.722 --> 00:04:32.022
away, though the Overview also refreshes on its own.

68
00:04:32.022 --> 00:04:33.312
That's the Overview.

69
00:04:33.312 --> 00:04:37.035
In the next videos, we'll go through each page in detail.

